--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,14 @@ make demo-data  # load sample rows for local browsing
 ```
 
 The API listens on the port given by `PORT`, default 3000.
+
+## Finding a free slot
+
+Instead of guessing a time and handling `409`, ask which slots are free:
+
+```bash
+curl "localhost:3000/bookings/availability?roomId=$ROOM&from=2026-01-05T09:00:00Z&to=2026-01-05T18:00:00Z&durationMinutes=60"
+```
+
+The answer lists the intervals left free by the active bookings of that room,
+never starting in the past, so a `startsAt` taken from a slot is bookable.
